const R={"4": "The shared quest-counter cycle records repeated household work; the third counter completes the challenge.", "14": "The stun counter and cantrip make Poseidon’s storm halt progress without a separate Foretell setup.", "48": "The Caryatid fixes mana immediately and doubles it once any permanent holds two counters, connecting ramp to the set’s existing counters.", "49": "A small flash flier makes the thunder an airborne omen; the enter trigger still carries the lightning strike.", "107": "At four mana the seven-toughness wall blocks the siege lane and its untapped ward protects the defenders behind it.", "113": "The whirlpool puts a creature back atop its owner’s library; scry adds a small rate improvement to the Griptide chassis.", "122": "The five-mana removal leaves a flying shade when a legendary figure falls, tying the effect to Hector’s death.", "144": "A redesigned obol denies graveyard passage and grants a modest ritual life reward without copying Soul-Guide Lantern’s card-draw option.", "149": "Heroic growth and a stealth evasion rider turn Athena’s guidance into a distinct night-raid twist.", "154": "The warning is now scrying after the counterspell; the set no longer asks this card to support Foretell.", "199": "Penelope gathers lore through patient turns and moves it to or from a Saga, linking her weaving to the set’s chapter machinery.", "201": "The exact shield art supports defensive equipment; four attack modes echo the cities, fields, sea, and heavens carved on it.", "204": "Damage to Patroclus prompts healing and strengthens a companion, following Achilles tending his wound in the selected art.", "210": "Sacrificing a creature or Food invokes Helios’s punishment; sacred Oxen gain ward without replaying every beat of the episode.", "211": "Flying fits Hermes’s winged identity and supplies a rare top-end flier while his exile-return role remains intact.", "213": "The Aura enchants the land beneath the rooted bed. Losing that land removes the bed, while hexproof, indestructible, ward and reunion draw reward keeping the home intact.", "215": "A single entrance choice grants one lasting divine path; Aphrodite’s repeatable small-creature appeal is the most aggressive RW option.", "217": "Face-down Manifest Fate entrants and permanents entering from exile both scry; the mana sink manifests fate and therefore triggers the first ability.", "218": "At two mana Moira sets up a graveyard-departure drain deck, with a cheaper late recursion sink distinct from the other virtues.", "219": "The bully name and combat pressure now fit the selected image of Eurymachus throwing a stool in the palace hall.", "222": "Three short chapters offer the Lotus-Eaters’ food, enchanted idleness and release with two creatures at most.", "232": "An offered creature yields Blood and life, surveil reads the omen, and the final chapter returns a small shade to the living.", "233": "The black Island Aura inverts the Mountain-dependent white exile card and borrows Deep-Cavern Bat’s temporary hand-exile pattern.", "237": "At two mana Kleos rewards legends dealing combat damage, then turns one legendary attacker into a trampling renown threat.", "239": "The orchard is now a land. It grows creatures with familiar +1/+1 counters and can be spent to recover a small permanent.", "240": "Casting enchantments or sorceries directly transforms one creature per turn, with no isolated craft-counter track.", "242": "The house is a land with a costly homecoming activation, making the household itself the source of restoration.", "243": "An opponent’s second spell can open the bag before its controller chooses to, making the wind’s setback volatile.", "245": "The Saga names Demodocus’s embedded song of Ares and Aphrodite in Odyssey VIII; its selected art depicts that tale rather than Penelope’s loom.", "246": "The sweeper becomes especially punitive after an opponent sacrifices a creature or Food, tying the extra damage to sacrilege.", "247": "One hidden card and a quiet end step replace the time-counter engine on Ogygia.", "249": "The Saga may detour from chapter II back to chapter I for another manifested fate or press on to the homecoming chapter on a later turn.", "269": "The white-black fixing land is a memorial to Hector’s burial at Troy; a Greek funerary soldier slab replaces Penelope’s chamber image.", "275": "Discarded stories accumulate shared lore counters, which later recover a spell or enchantment.", "279": "A communal vessel counts as both Food and Clue and can be spent for nourishment or a card.", "289": "Charge counters now represent Achilles’s stored anger without a unique wrath-counter type.", "297": "Charge counters now track the repeated return of cards from the graveyard without a unique memory-counter type."};
